  "final_message": "I'm pausing before I change anything, because removing the field from the event conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n`channel` is part of the published `OrderPlaced` payload (`src/core/events.ts:16`, `:50`). billing-service and analytics-ingest consume that event from other repositories. I can only see this repo, so I can't confirm that neither of them reads `channel`. Deleting a field from a deployed event can break a consumer that still parses it, and ARCH-4 requires removals to go through deprecation. The same applies to `GET /orders/{id}` (ARCH-8): web-storefront gets the order model there. `channel` isn't in the 201 response shape today, but I'd want to check that before touching the model.\n\nOptions:\n\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).**\n   - Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on the event.\n   - Make it optional on the `POST /orders` input, so callers can stop sending it.\n   - Keep populating it on the event.\n   - Tell billing-service and analytics-ingest that it will be removed.\n   - Remove it once both confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it now from the order model and the input only.** The `OrderPlaced` event would keep emitting `channel`, which means the order would need to retain the value.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** Choose this if you've already confirmed with both consumer teams that they don't read it and you want to override ARCH-4 for this change.\n\nWhich one should I do? If you have confirmation from both consumer teams, tell me and I'll go with option 3.",
